SM(617,{"n":"Revelation 7.9-8.13","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Revelation 7.9-8.13.mp3","d":2339.8,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.96,"So verse 9."],[22.32,"After these things."],[33.68,"Standing before the throne and before the Lamb, clothed with white robes, with palm branches in their hands."],[41.6,"So he's got okay."],[45.28,"So now there's all these people."],[47.57,"From all over."],[48.77,"They've all got the white robes."],[50.13,"Remember the white robes from back in the letters to the churches."],[53.03,"This is what you get when you overcome."],[55.51,"This is what the elders had."],[57.68,"The elders where there were some humans up there."],[60.04,"This is now all of these folks."],[65.37,"And the palm branches are symbols of victory."],[69.87,"The one to him who overcomes."],[72.25,"That refrain from the letters."],[75.05,"And crying out with a loud voice, saying, Salvation belongs to our God who sits on the throne and to the Lamb."],[83.13,"All the angels stood around the throne, and the elders and the four living creatures and fell on their faces before the throne and worshipped God, saying, Amen."],[92.17,"Blessing and glory and wisdom, thanksgiving and honor and power and might be to our God forever and ever."],[99.05,"Amen. Okay. So we had the beginning of the judgment when the sixth seal was open."],[108.13,"Then we press pause."],[109.43,"Time out. The angels hold back."],[112.82,"Sort of the destructive forces."],[114.66,"So that we can, all of the people of God can be sealed."],[118.68,"And now they're all gathered together into that heavenly worship we saw before."],[124.1,"Everybody's now brought in."],[126.74,"All those people who were who were sealed."],[131.62,"Verse 13. Then one of the elders answered, saying to me, Who are these arrayed in white robes, and where did they come from?"],[139.54,"And I said to him, Sir, you know."],[143.46,"Umtice again, it's just one of the elders"],[149.98,"It doesn't say who could be himself."],[152.46,"He could be talking to himself again."],[157.23,"So he said to me, These are the ones who came out of the great tribulation and washed their robes and made them white in the blood of the Lamb."],[167.07,"Therefore, they are before the throne of God, and serve him day and night in his temple, and he who sits on the throne will dwell among them."],[176.19,"Okay, so a couple things there."],[180.51,"So the first one is the Great Tribulation, and now I'm going to disappoint everyone again."],[185.55,"Because I know we've been told by some of our American eschatologically oriented friends that the Great Tribulation is something, maybe a seven-year period that is sometime in the future."],[200.56,"So the basic problem with this is that the book of Daniel talks about the Great Tribulation in the present tense."],[212.96,"Daniel talks about it in the present tense."],[218.64,"So that means this isn't something that's going to happen in particular in the future."],[227.6,"And if you look at that Great Tribulation language, which is not only in Daniel, it also appears in other Second Temple literature, even appears in the Dead Sea Scrolls."],[236.81,"That is a way of describing the period of time from the quote unquote end of the exile."],[246.47,"Because after 70 years, a group of uh the remnant of Judah get to go back."],[256.49,"They establish Judea as first a Persian province, and then it becomes a Seleucid Greek province, and then it becomes a Roman province."],[265.51,"They're allowed to go back to South."],[266.87,"So they don't all go back."],[268.44,"A bunch stay in Mesopotamia, a bunch stay in Egypt."],[271.6,"People are scattered all over the place."],[274.48,"But they get to go back and establish that."],[276.32,"But the presence of God never returns to the temple when they rededicate it."],[281.6,"But equally as importantly, shall we say, they're under this foreign oppression."],[288.42,"So the Persians don't treat them that badly, but that doesn't last that long."],[292.28,"Alexander the Great comes through and makes fairly short work of the Persians."],[297.72,"And Seleucus is given Syria, ends up getting Judea, and the Greeks, especially under Antiochus IV Epiphanes, brutally, oppress and martyr."],[311.88,"The uh the people of Judea."],[315.52,"The Romans uh get basically invited in in order to try and get help them get free and stay free uh from the Seleucids."],[326.04,"Uh the Maccabees, the Hasmonians, sign a uh treaty with Rome, mutual protection treaty with the city of Rome, and that doesn't work out so good for them."],[338.26,"Uh they end up getting annexed by Rome."],[341.11,"So the Great Tribulation is a way of referring to that period."],[345.33,"That whole period where the exile kinda ended, but it really didn't."],[354.55,"It really didn't."],[356.95,"And so they were looking forward to, from the Jewish perspective, they were looking forward to the coming of the Messianic Age that would represent an end to that great tribulation."],[373.18,"That's why the idea of the Romans getting overthrown was so tightly connected."],[379.58,"We're not going to be under foreign oppression anymore."],[384.03,"We're going to really be back in the land with our own king."],[388.41,"Able to purify the temple and do the things correctly, and everything will be back the way it should be, like it was when David was king."],[397.23,"That's sort of how they're they're looking at it."],[399.79,"And in that it's not that, it is this great tribulation."],[403.83,"So they didn't believe God was in the temple of extended."],[407.83,"Well, no, he hadn't so when when you read the dedication of the tabernacle, dedication of the first temple, there is this appearance of what's called the Theophanic glory cloud."],[420.64,"Comes rushing into the there's these visible signs and all these things that happen."],[425.28,"That's not recorded as happening when they rebuilt it under uh Nehemiah."],[430.56,"Uh then of course it gets wrecked again by um and the Ark of the Covenant isn't there."],[437.76,"They don't have the Ark of the Covenant anymore."],[440.08,"Um it gets wrecked again by Antiochus Epiphanes, who comes in and desecrates it, sacrifices pigs on the altar to Zen."],[447.56,"When the Maccabees rededicate it, you get, you know, the oil that lasts like eight days instead of instead of one."],[457.98,"So like we have a festival to celebrate a really good quality product."],[462.46,"Um but uh but that's it."],[465.02,"I mean, that's the miracle that happens when it gets rededicated."],[468.36,"There's not this big display of power."],[473.0,"When Pompey comes in to annex Judea, he marches right into the Holy of Holies and is kind of blown away by the fact that there's nothing there."],[484.28,"Because he's expecting to find some elaborate idols, some kind of something."],[490.05,"He walks in and it's a big empty room, basically."],[495.01,"So he he kind of that and so that actually that actually helped them with the Romans, because then the Romans are like, ah, they worship God solamente."],[502.63,"Only with their minds."],[504.39,"This must be some refined religion."],[507.23,"Um, but Bob, because Bombe's confused."],[509.95,"But he he walks right in there, he doesn't drop dead, nothing happens to him."],[514.83,"Touching the Ark of the Covenant used to be fatal."],[517.31,"Yeah, oh yeah."],[518.03,"Yeah, they'd have an abahu."],[519.65,"Like you couldn't get anywhere near."],[521.19,"Like so there's this awareness that they have that things still aren't right."],[528.39,"I have a follow-up question"],[531.19,"What rends the veil of the temple in Christ does well it's opened up to dis sort of display that there's nothing there."],[544.13,"To everyone. Yeah, yeah."],[547.87,"And so the there are various various Jewish sects have various reasonings as to why that is."],[555.08,"Generally it's something needs to happen."],[557.64,"Foreign domination needs to go away, or it's because the Sadducees are completely corrupt."],[563.5,"And this is the wrong high priestly family."],[565.98,"So if we get rid of them and restore the true priesthood."],[569.68,"There's various versions."],[571.53,"Um of what it will be, but sort of that's part of the mark, then that the tribulation is over the messianic age has come."],[580.79,"And so there's also when it tears, that's part of the whole inversion that happens, where the Messiah does come and they crucify him."],[590.65,"And instead of the presence of God coming back, it rips right from top to bottom, and there's nothing there."],[598.25,"I mean, in going to be a good thing."],[600.89,"Yeah. So there that all sort of ends up getting the expectation, at least."],[608.17,"Gets gets inverted."],[610.22,"So all that is to say is that St."],[613.66,"John is actually extending the Great Tribulation beyond, because by the time he's writing this, the temple doesn't exist."],[626.31,"Temple of Jerusalem doesn't exist at the time he's having this vision and this is being written."],[632.04,"So the physical temple of Jerusalem, at least."],[634.94,"Because he's going to mention the temple here, but he's not talking about the physical one."],[638.84,"Um physical temple's been destroyed."],[644.09,"He's extending the Great Tribulation forward until the end."],[649.38,"So he's saying the hardships being faced by the Christians, him being in exile on Patmas."],[656.68,"The people being martyred."],[658.2,"That's all part of the Great Tribulation"],[663.74,"So we have every generation now."],[666.06,"Yes. Yes. Yeah."],[675.51,"So he's extending that."],[678.69,"And taking it from, again, just the Judeans to applying to, again, the people of God."],[687.22,"Which for him is Christians, which includes Judean Christians and everybody else."],[695.03,"Um. And so that will continue until. right Christ's return when everything is set right and re-established"],[705.07,"So these folks have the white robes."],[709.47,"Remember, we get we're picking up on the language from before, to hit to him who overcomes."],[715.81,"So these are the people who have emerged victorious from the Great Tribulation."],[721.65,"That's why they've got the white robes, that's why they've got the palm branches."],[725.91,"They've emerged victorious from the Great Tribulation that we've all right been through."],[733.16,"Um which the the seals we saw, like the four horsemen, that's part of it."],[744.03,"What's going on in this age."],[746.09,"That's part of the great the great tribulation."],[751.45,"And notice, they've washed, the robes are white because they've been washed in the blood of the lamb."],[758.53,"Washing something in blood usually we don't associate with making it white."],[762.89,"But the point here is we talked last time a little bit about the Day of Atonement."],[770.3,"Remember, the blood was taken and used to purify, the physical things."],[776.1,"The physical elements."],[777.3,"Blood was also used in the ordination uh ritual."],[781.4,"But so what was the why did these things have to constantly be purified?"],[785.04,"Was the whole purpose of the Torah and all of these regulations?"],[788.08,"All the washings people had to do, the purifying of everything with blood on the Day of Atonement."],[793.28,"It was so that people who were otherwise sinful could come into the presence of God."],[798.08,"So God could continue to live in the camp or in the temple in the midst of a people who were sinful."],[805.45,"The sin had to be sort of managed with this system."],[809.59,"And so the blood of Christ now, superior to the blood of a goat."],[814.17,"You don't have to do it every year, you don't have to do it."],[817.19,"It's once and for all has purified them and made them able."],[822.44,"You notice to serve day and night in his temple."],[829.05,"So it's not like the priesthood of the Torah, where before the time of their service came, they had to go through all of the purification rituals again to be able to come safely into the presence of God."],[840.49,"And they had to abstain from their wives, and they had to change what they ate, and they had to do all the washings and they."],[846.78,"Now, day and night, they're in God's presence in heaven, because they've been purified once and for all with the blood of Christ."],[861.1,"Verse 16 they shall neither hunger anymore nor thirst anymore."],[865.18,"The sun shall not strike them nor any heat."],[867.98,"For the lamb who is in the midst of the throne will shepherd. them and lead them to living fountains of waters"],[874.9,"And God will wipe away every tear from their eyes."],[878.47,"Tribulation over. And notice again, they're reigning and serving as priests."],[890.37,"The presence of God."],[892.53,"On this ongoing basis."],[893.97,"We talked before about what priests do."],[895.81,"They offer sacrifices."],[897.17,"These folks aren't offering sacrifices anymore."],[899.57,"They offer prayers and intercessions."],[903.25,"So this is what the saints in glory are doing again here, according to the book of Revelation."],[914.49,"Excuse me. Chapter 8."],[919.21,"Now we get to the seventh seal."],[921.29,"So now we unpause."],[923.61,"We were paused there for a minute."],[927.21,"Now seal seven."],[929.05,"When he opened the seventh seal, there was silence in heaven for about half an hour."],[935.61,"And I saw the seven angels who stand before God, and to them were given seven trumpets."],[942.49,"Remember how I said there's these cycles in everything St."],[946.81,"John writes? Well, here's another one."],[948.27,"We get to the seventh seal open, and now, okay, hand out seven trumpets."],[952.12,"To seven angels."],[953.4,"So we're going to start another cycle of seven."],[958.96,"Then another angel, having a golden censor, came and stood at the altar."],[964.8,"He was given much incense that he should offer it with the prayers of all the saints upon the golden altar which was before the throne."],[974.96,"So we have this heavenly altar."],[979.57,"This uh this golden altar."],[981.81,"What kind of altar is it?"],[983.33,"Based on what we just had."],[985.33,"It's an altar of incense."],[987.59,"So there there''ss there's multiple altars, in in the the Torah."],[991.91,"So you've got the altar of incense, which was a horned altar, it had like horns at the four corners, that was in the holy place, in the tabernacle, and then in the temple."],[1000.87,"in So it was sort of front of the curtain to the most holy place."],[1000.95,"the And that was the place where priests did most of their business."],[1010.27,"Because at morning and evening, this is the first commandment about worship in the Torah."],[1014.75,"Morning and evening they come and offer incense on the altar of incense with prayers."],[1020.76,"This is where we get Matins and Vespers."],[1024.76,"Um the uh the altar of burnt offering, which is what we usually think of as the altar for sacrifices, was in the courtyard."],[1033.72,"It was outside the tabernacle proper or the temple proper."],[1038.2,"For reasons that are kind of obvious, having to do with huge amounts of greasy smoke."],[1042.7,"For burning burning animals."],[1044.56,"Sometimes whole uh didn't work so well inside a tent of goat hair right um so that was outside right so this is before the throne right where in the tabernacle or the temple or our church for that matter is the throne of God back in the back of the most holy place and the altar the altar of incense is his footstool our church is set up the same way."],[1079.09,"The high place behind the altar, is where the throne of God is."],[1083.71,"Th'eres places in the liturgy where we bless the high place."],[1087.52,"That's why when I go back behind the altar, when we're about to do the readings, that's why I don't stand in the middle."],[1096.48,"Stand off to the side."],[1097.94,"Because Christ is in the middle enthroned there."],[1101.46,"With the altar as his footstool."],[1103.3,"So it's the same setup."],[1104.26,"So when he sees it in heaven, altar."],[1107.83,"No curtain in heaven."],[1110.59,"Altar of incense."],[1113.63,"In front of it, which is made of solid gold."],[1116.99,"And so the way the incense altar worked is that you had coal burning there all the time."],[1124.25,"And then you would offer incense on it."],[1126.89,"And then sensors were used to take the incense other places."],[1129.45,"take. So you would a coal from the altar and put it in the sensor"],[1136.69,"And then take incense from the altar and put it in the sensor."],[1139.57,"And now you've made it mobile."],[1141.57,"So that you could take that incense that's being offered to God, and you could take it and use it to purify the space."],[1149.09,"You could take it outside, to purify the space."],[1153.99,"And so this is the image of what's happening here with this angel."],[1157.19,"This angel has this gold sensor."],[1159.93,"And he's taking from the altar."],[1163.11,"The coal and the incense."],[1164.55,"And that incense, is being offered up with the prayers of all the saints."],[1171.18,"But why is he taking would he take that in a sensor?"],[1172.54,"take He's going to it, use it to purify some space."],[1180.76,"So, what is purifying the space?"],[1183.16,"What is the incense here?"],[1184.52,"What did we just get told it was?"],[1186.52,"It's the prayers of all the saints."],[1191.64,"So the prayers of the saints are now going to purify something."],[1200.36,"These are the same saints we were just talking about, who are there who are part of the worship, who are serving and offering their prayers and intercessions."],[1210.04,"Excuse me. Verse 4."],[1214.12,"And the smoke of the incense, with the prayers of the saints. ascended before God from the angel's hand"],[1220.72,"Then the angel took the censer, filled it with fire from the altar, and threw it to the earth."],[1226.56,"And there were noises, thunderings, lightnings, and an earthquake."],[1232.56,"So that's pretty epic."],[1234.16,"Sensor smash. So what's he purifying with the censor?"],[1241.54,"The earth. The earth."],[1244.82,"That's what he's using the incense to purify."],[1248.15,"Kind of a violent purification."],[1250.63,"But so that's the idea."],[1252.47,"But again, what is the incense?"],[1254.71,"It's the prayers of the saints."],[1257.87,"So the imagery we saw with the seals was about authority."],[1263.67,"It was about Christ taking back authority over the whole creation."],[1268.49,"Authority, ultimately, authority to judge."],[1272.01,"Now we're going to have another set of seven that we're approaching with the seven trumpets."],[1278.25,"This one isn't going to be focused on Christ's authority and his rule."],[1282.41,"This one is going to be focused more on ritual purification."],[1290.7,"Turning the creation, the earth, back into sacred space."],[1297.58,"Which it was originally."],[1300.06,"When you read Genesis 1, the seven days are structured, are patterned after uh temple dedication rituals in the ancient Near East."],[1314.82,"When on the seventh day God rests, we tend to read that overly literally."],[1319.32,"Like God needed a break, he'd been working real hard, so he took it easy for one day."],[1324.28,"But that rests is actually sat down, i.e. he's enthroned at the end of it within his temple, which is the whole cosmos."],[1334.92,"Okay. Temple got defiled."],[1337.4,"Temple's not doing so great right now if we look at the whole world as supposed to be sacred space."],[1342.66,"But so that process is now beginning."],[1346.9,"Because previous to this, we had the saints in heaven"],[1351.23,"The temple of God is now this heavenly temple still, of which the one on earth was a copy."],[1357.87,"But what we're going to see as we progress now is that the earth is now going to become the place where God dwells, the whole creation, not just the heavens."],[1374.03,"Verse 6. So the seven angels who had the seven trumpets prepared themselves to sound."],[1383.31,"Verse 7. The first angel sounded, meaning blew his trumpet."],[1387.68,"And I well, I don't know for sure, but some of you may be picturing like the long skinny trumpet like on top of a Mormon church or something uh gotta roll back this is more like a shofar right this is this is a like a ram's horn like a shofar that they're blowing the first angel sounded and hail and fire followed mingled with blood and they were thrown to the earth and a third of the trees were burned up and all green grass was burned up okay so um did anybody uh find uh did anybody recognize that phrase there?"],[1437.92,"Hail and fire mingled with blood."],[1441.6,"Where that might have appeared in the Bible before."],[1446.16,"No? It's fire from heaven."],[1451.28,"Egypt. Egypt. Plague on Egypt."],[1454.72,"Remember the hail?"],[1456.48,"And the fire that came down together?"],[1460.0,"On Egypt. And notice it takes out a third of the uh vegetable life."],[1469.01,"And all the grass."],[1470.29,"Yeah. Verse 8."],[1473.85,"Then the second angel sounded, and something like a great mountain burning with fire was thrown into the the se seaa. and a third of became blood"],[1482.97,"And a third of the living creatures in the sea died, and a third of the ships were destroyed."],[1487.77,"Is that reminiscent anybody of anything?"],[1491.21,"Yeah, but plague on Egypt."],[1493.26,"Turned the water to blood."],[1498.94,"Verse 10 then the third angel sounded."],[1503.42,"And a great star fell from heaven, burning like a torch, and it fell on a third of the rivers and on the springs of water."],[1510.94,"The name of the star is wormwood."],[1512.86,"A third of the waters became wormwood."],[1515.5,"And many men died from the water because it was made bitter."],[1520.54,"That's not directly one of the plagues on Egypt, but remember when they were wandering in Sinai?"],[1524.38,"They come and they find the bitter water"],[1529.94,"Moses throws the wood into it, and it becomes sweet."],[1538.59,"And notice a third."],[1540.76,"Again of the waters."],[1546.92,"Verse 12. Then the fourth angel sounded, and a third of the sun was struck, a third of the moon, and a third of the stars, so that a third of them were darkened."],[1556.12,"A third of the day did not shine, and likewise the night."],[1563.64,"Remember the darkness over Egypt?"],[1567.66,"One of the plagues."],[1569.74,"But we've got that third metaphor."],[1573.1,"And notice this can't be all just going in order."],[1577.28,"Because remember sixth seal."],[1580.4,"Remember? All the stars fell out of the sky."],[1583.84,"The sun was darkened and the moon turned to blood."],[1586.56,"And now it's back at only a third."],[1589.34,"So it's literally impossible to read this as like a literal succession of future events."],[1595.76,"We've got these cycles that overlap."],[1598.28,"You guys have disciplines."],[1599.56,"Thanks when watching you."],[1605.6,"Verse 13. And I looked and I heard an angel flying through the midst of heaven, saying with a loud voice, Whoa, woe, woe to the inhabitants of the earth, because of the remaining blasts of the trumpet of the three angels who are about to sound."],[1621.96,"So we'll pause there."],[1624.28,"So now we get this."],[1625.88,"Oh, you're really in trouble, it's about to get worse."],[1632.32,"So um, as I said, we're coming through now from the perspective of purification."],[1642.98,"This doesn't look like purification, this looks like the opposite."],[1645.94,"Yeah Yeah. Purification with an engine."],[1650.02,"Um, because things keep getting smote."],[1654.84,"At least a third of them."],[1656.8,"Um we've got stuff falling out of the sky."],[1661.06,"Mountains and stars and meteors and right, all these things."],[1666.26,"But that third number is important."],[1670.58,"Because um, well, there's no spoilers, people have read this before."],[1677.54,"So when we get into Revelation chapter 12."],[1680.52,"When we get to chapter 12, which we won't tonight, uh, but when we get to chapter 12, we're gonna see that the dragon, the serpent, the devil, throws a third of the stars of heaven down."],[1695.4,"And we're gonna see some interesting. things there in terms of that number and that that third"],[1704.08,"But these thirds that we're seeing and the judgments we're seeing, and the fact that they're associated with the plagues in Egypt is a tip-off."],[1712.96,"Because before the final plague comes on Egypt."],[1718.18,"The Passover. The death of the firstborn of Egypt."],[1722.04,"God comes to Moses and tells him what he's doing."],[1726.76,"He says he's going to do two things that night."],[1732.2,"The first thing he says is that night he's going to judge all the gods of Egypt."],[1738.13,"Which is a good tip-off that from the perspective of Exodus at least, they're not fictional characters."],[1744.59,"God doesn't need to judge the Marvel Cinematic Universe."],[1748.11,"He doesn't need to judge Star Wars."],[1751.37,"It's fiction. Okay."],[1753.45,"So the gods of Egypt are not fictional."],[1755.77,"They include Pharaoh."],[1757.79,"But there are demonic forces, there are demonic powers that have control of Egypt."],[1763.37,"That the people of Egypt have followed, have worshipped, have given control over them and over Egypt."],[1769.69,"And God is coming to judge them because he's going to liberate not just his people from them, but potentially any of the Egyptians who want to."],[1779.41,"Because the second thing he says he's going to do is he's going to make a distinction between the people of Egypt and the people of Israel."],[1790.37,"So what does he mean by that."],[1791.9,"Because obviously there was already kind of a distinction."],[1794.99,"Um previous to that, when you read about the plagues, the plagues didn't fall on the place, the land of Goshen, the place where the Israelites were living."],[1809.52,"So there was darkness over everywhere except where the Israelites were living."],[1815.14,"The water all turned to blood except where the Israelites were living."],[1818.5,"Frogs everywhere except where the Israelites were living."],[1822.07,"But we know from various parts of the story. that the Israelites and the Egyptians were living right next to each other"],[1830.27,"It wasn't like only Israelites live here, Egyptians live in other places."],[1835.15,"So the Egyptians who happened to live in Israelite neighborhoods lucked out, but it came to plagues."],[1840.64,"Like they got away, you know, scot free."],[1844.32,"But now there's gonna be a distinction."],[1860.4,"He gives them the instructions."],[1862.8,"And there are gonna be people who follow that and people who don't follow that."],[1867.04,"And so that night, everyone who follows that. is an Israelite"],[1874.28,"Doesn't matter their DNA, doesn't matter their skin color, doesn't matter any of that."],[1880.33,"Anybody who doesn't follow that, those instructions, is an Egyptian."],[1886.65,"Again, doesn't matter their DNA, doesn't matter their skin color, doesn't matter who their great great great great grandfather was."],[1895.29,"If you celebrate the Passover, you're now an Israelite."],[1898.91,"And this carries over through the rest of the Torah."],[1902.45,"The way you become an Israelite is you go and you get circumcised and then you celebrate the Passover."],[1908.61,"It's right there in the Torah."],[1909.89,"That makes you now you're an Israelite."],[1911.73,"Doesn't matter where you're from."],[1913.75,"If you're a woman, you can't get circumcised, so you marry a circumcised man and eat the Passover."],[1920.67,"That's what that's what brings you in."],[1923.05,"So that's how this distinction is made between the people who are going to belong to God and the people who belong to those other spirits that are being judged."],[1938.86,"And so what St."],[1940.86,"John wants us to think here is of the plagues on Egypt and on that distinction."],[1946.8,"This is why we have a third."],[1949.12,"Because there's a separation happening here."],[1954.08,"When God created originally, and that was his temple, as we were just saying, what was the first thing that defiled it?"],[1968.92,"The devil. Got the snake walker."],[1974.09,"It's not a literal snake."],[1975.38,"The serpent. The devil."],[1977.58,"Is in there."],[1980.14,"So not only should Adam and Eve not have sort of gone with him on the whole tree thing, but they should have run him out of town."],[1993.64,"They should have protected and purified that sacred space."],[1997.16,"Didn't Should have thrown him out."],[2002.62,"Sided with him instead."],[2005.59,"And then through their death, they he ended up getting ownership rights."],[2011.83,"So to purify the creationist sacred space, we've got to separate who's on which side."],[2024.6,"And if our number coming up in chapter 12 for the number of demonic spirits that are out there is a third."],[2033.69,"Then people who have allegiance to them probably also going to be about a third."],[2039.85,"And so the plagues are falling on them"],[2045.69,"The plagues are falling on them."],[2048.81,"But if we think back to the plagues on Egypt."],[2055.57,"That distinction wasn't made till the very last one."],[2060.05,"Which means what?"],[2061.89,"Which means if you're an Egyptian and you watch the first nine plagues, unfold, and you watch Moses confronting Pharaoh, and you say, you know what?"],[2073.19,"I am Yahweh, the God of Israel, is the one I want to follow."],[2078.49,"I think I want to be one of these people."],[2081.21,"I think I want to leave Egypt with them."],[2082.33,"Then when the Passover comes, you have the opportunity to do that"],[2092.45,"Yeah. And we're told a mixed multitude comes out of Egypt."],[2095.17,"Oh, okay. They're people with Egyptian names."],[2098.69,"Like Moses. Yeah, yeah."],[2100.45,"But not just Moses."],[2102.21,"And not just Moses' immediate family who all have Egyptian names."],[2106.05,"Um. But uh, so so, yeah, they're ethnically completely mixed from a DNA type perspective."],[2116.05,"God is is creating a new people that didn't exist before."],[2120.93,"He says he's doing that."],[2122.97,"Um so that means those nine plagues could potentially have driven any of those people to repentance."],[2133.78,"Because I mean, why why why do this in sequence?"],[2139.32,"We need to purify the earth."],[2140.68,"Okay, that's easy."],[2141.8,"Kill all the wicked."],[2145.16,"Done. Purified. But that's not how God does it."],[2152.21,"Step by step."],[2156.58,"And the people are observing."],[2159.07,"That angel with the woes is calling out to somebody."],[2164.32,"Warning somebody about what. that it's about to get worse"],[2168.93,"Now's the time to switch sides."],[2170.95,"Now's the time to get over it."],[2173.27,"So this is still, as we go, just like we saw with the seven seals, and Christ taking his authority back."],[2182.29,"Every judgment is a call to repentance."],[2185.86,"It has the potential, the tribulation, the sorry, has the ability to become the cause of repentance for people."],[2192.66,"So that they can end up being part of that number with the white robes."],[2197.18,"And as we cycle through again now from this other perspective of sacred space, the same thing is true."],[2205.6,"The same thing is true."],[2207.52,"That's why God. doesn't just boom, it's done"],[2211.82,"But he extends this period to give these opportunities for repentance."],[2221.18,"And there are a lot of fascinating things, as an aside before we finish."],[2225.26,"A lot of fascinating things with that a third number in history."],[2230.27,"Like, it turns up a lot."],[2232.19,"The black plague."],[2234.91,"You know, the 30 Years' War killed about a third."],[2239.41,"Um so that that uh interestingly, that third number pops up here and there."],[2244.77,"And of course, as we said last time, there were people at all those times saying, Look, a third of Europe was like this is it."],[2254.38,"Um, but again, it's not it's not literal, it's supposed to point us to."],[2260.64,"The fact that there are other spirits other than the Holy Spirit that are animating people and that people are following in this world."],[2272.53,"And God is not just about destroying them and punishing them for it, but he's about giving them the opportunity to repent until he reaches that point that we started out talking about tonight, where it needs to be brought to an end, and the time for repentance is closed."],[2290.5,"But so that's what we see unfolding with these first four trumpets."],[2295.18,"And uh when we come back next time, next week, same bat time, same bat channel."],[2301.42,"We'll pick up at chapter nine and do the uh the final trumpets."],[2306.86,"And then we'll get into some more stuff."],[2309.5,"Enoch and Elijah showing back up, people eating books."],[2313.74,"Thank you, everybody."],[2317.34,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2324.7,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2330.06,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":20.96,"lv":2,"h":"7:9-12 - The great multitude","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 9</b>: crowd <b>from all over</b>, before throne and Lamb</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>White robes</b> - back in the <b>letters to the churches</b></li><li class=\"d1\">what you get when you <b>overcome</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>elders</b> had them - some humans up there; now <b>all these folks</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Palm branches</b> = symbols of <b>victory</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"to him who <b>overcomes</b>\" - the refrain from the letters</li><li class=\"d0\">Cry: <b>\"Salvation belongs to our God\"</b> and the Lamb</li><li class=\"d0\">Angels, elders, four living creatures <b>fall on faces</b>: <b>Amen</b>, blessing, glory, wisdom, thanksgiving, honor, power, might</li><li class=\"d0\">Recap: <b>sixth seal</b> = beginning of judgment</li><li class=\"d1\">then <b>pause</b> - \"time out\", angels hold back destructive forces</li><li class=\"d1\">so all God's people can be <b>sealed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">now all the sealed <b>gathered into heavenly worship</b></li></ul>"},{"t":131.62,"lv":2,"h":"7:13-17 - Who are these in white?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 13</b>: one of the elders asks John: who are these, where from?</li><li class=\"d0\">John: \"Sir, you know\" - again \"just <b>one of the elders</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't say who - could be <b>talking to himself</b> again</li><li class=\"d0\">Answer: they <b>came out of the great tribulation</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>washed their robes</b>, made white in the <b>blood of the Lamb</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Therefore before the throne, <b>serve day and night in his temple</b></li><li class=\"d1\">he who sits on the throne <b>dwells among them</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Two things to note - first: the <b>Great Tribulation</b></li></ul>"},{"t":176.19,"lv":3,"h":"The Great Tribulation is not future","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Disappoint everyone again\": American <b>eschatological</b> friends say a <b>seven-year future</b> period</li><li class=\"d0\">Problem: <b>Daniel</b> talks about it in the <b>present tense</b></li><li class=\"d1\">so not something that happens in particular in the future</li><li class=\"d0\">Language also in <b>Second Temple literature</b>, even <b>Dead Sea Scrolls</b></li><li class=\"d0\">= the period from the <b>\"end of the exile\"</b> onward</li><li class=\"d0\">After <b>70 years</b> a remnant of Judah goes back</li><li class=\"d1\">Judea: <b>Persian</b> province, then <b>Seleucid Greek</b>, then <b>Roman</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not all return - many stay in <b>Mesopotamia</b>, <b>Egypt</b>; people scattered</li><li class=\"d0\">Return, but <b>God's presence never returns</b> to the temple when rededicated</li></ul>"},{"t":227.6,"lv":3,"h":"Foreign oppression after the return","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Persians didn't treat them badly - didn't last</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Alexander the Great</b> makes \"short work\" of Persians</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Seleucus</b> gets Syria, ends up with Judea</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Antiochus IV Epiphanes</b> - brutally oppresses and martyrs Judea</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Romans</b> basically <b>invited in</b> to help them get and stay free of Seleucids</li><li class=\"d1\">Maccabees/<b>Hasmoneans</b> sign <b>mutual protection treaty</b> with Rome - \"doesn't work out so good\"</li><li class=\"d1\">end up <b>annexed</b> by Rome</li><li class=\"d0\">Great Tribulation = <b>that whole period</b> - exile kind of ended, \"but it really didn't\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Jewish hope: <b>Messianic Age</b> ends it</li><li class=\"d1\">why overthrowing <b>Romans</b> was so tied in</li><li class=\"d1\">own <b>king</b>, purify the temple, \"like it was when <b>David</b> was king\"</li></ul>"},{"t":403.83,"lv":3,"h":"The temple without glory","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Did they think God was in the rebuilt temple? No</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Tabernacle and first temple</b> dedication: <b>theophanic glory cloud</b>, visible signs</li><li class=\"d1\">not recorded under <b>Nehemiah</b>; <b>Ark of the Covenant</b> gone</li><li class=\"d0\">Wrecked again by <b>Antiochus Epiphanes</b></li><li class=\"d1\">desecrated, <b>pigs sacrificed to Zeus</b> on the altar</li><li class=\"d1\">Maccabees rededicate: miracle = <b>oil lasting eight days</b> - \"a festival to celebrate a really good quality product\"</li><li class=\"d1\">no big display of power</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Pompey</b> marches into the <b>Holy of Holies</b>, \"blown away\" - nothing there</li><li class=\"d1\">expected idols; a big empty room</li><li class=\"d1\">Romans: worship God \"only with their minds\" - refined religion</li><li class=\"d1\">he <b>doesn't drop dead</b> - touching the Ark used to be <b>fatal</b> (Abihu...)</li><li class=\"d0\">→ awareness that <b>things still aren't right</b></li></ul>"},{"t":528.39,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: the veil of the temple","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: what rends the <b>veil</b> at Christ's death? - opened to display <b>nothing there</b>, to everyone</li><li class=\"d0\">Jewish sects had various reasons why still in tribulation</li><li class=\"d1\">needs <b>foreign domination</b> gone</li><li class=\"d1\">or <b>Sadducees</b> corrupt, <b>wrong high-priestly family</b> - restore the true priesthood</li><li class=\"d0\">Expected sign: <b>tribulation over, messianic age come</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Veil tearing = part of the <b>inversion</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Messiah comes and they <b>crucify him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">instead of God's presence coming back, veil <b>rips top to bottom</b> - nothing there</li><li class=\"d1\">expectation <b>inverted</b></li></ul>"},{"t":610.22,"lv":2,"h":"John extends the Great Tribulation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">By the time John writes, <b>temple of Jerusalem doesn't exist</b></li><li class=\"d1\">he'll mention \"the temple\" - <b>not the physical one</b></li><li class=\"d0\">John <b>extends the Great Tribulation forward until the end</b></li><li class=\"d1\">hardships of Christians, John in <b>exile on Patmos</b>, martyrs</li><li class=\"d1\">\"every generation now\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moves from just <b>Judeans</b> to the <b>people of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= Christians, <b>Judean Christians and everybody else</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Continues until <b>Christ's return</b> - everything set right and re-established</li><li class=\"d0\">Seals - <b>four horsemen</b> etc. - part of what goes on in <b>this age</b> = the tribulation</li></ul>"},{"t":705.07,"lv":2,"h":"7:14-15 - Washed in the Lamb's blood","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">White robes and palms: picking up <b>\"to him who overcomes\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they've <b>emerged victorious</b> from the Great Tribulation</li><li class=\"d0\">Robes white <b>because washed in blood</b> - odd; we don't associate blood with white</li><li class=\"d0\">Recall <b>Day of Atonement</b> (last time)</li><li class=\"d1\">blood used to <b>purify physical things</b>; also in <b>ordination</b> ritual</li><li class=\"d1\">purpose of Torah, washings, blood: so <b>sinful people could come into God's presence</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God lives in camp/temple among sinners - sin <b>\"managed\"</b> by the system</li><li class=\"d0\">Blood of Christ <b>superior to blood of a goat</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not every year - <b>once and for all</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"Serve day and night\"</b> - not like Torah priests</li><li class=\"d1\">had to repeat purifications, <b>abstain from wives</b>, change diet, washings</li><li class=\"d1\">now in God's presence in heaven <b>continually</b></li></ul>"},{"t":861.1,"lv":3,"h":"7:16-17 - Tribulation over","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 16</b>: no more <b>hunger or thirst</b>; no sun or heat</li><li class=\"d0\">The <b>Lamb in the midst of the throne</b> shepherds them to <b>living fountains of water</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>God wipes away every tear</b> - \"tribulation over\"</li><li class=\"d0\">They <b>reign and serve as priests</b> in God's presence, ongoing</li><li class=\"d1\">priests offer <b>sacrifices</b> - not anymore</li><li class=\"d1\">offer <b>prayers and intercessions</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= what <b>saints in glory</b> do in Revelation</li></ul>"},{"t":914.49,"lv":2,"h":"8:1-5 - Seventh seal, golden censer","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Chapter 8</b>: <b>seventh seal</b> - \"now we unpause\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Silence in heaven</b> about half an hour</li><li class=\"d0\">Seven angels before God given <b>seven trumpets</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Another of John's <b>cycles</b>: seventh seal opens → seven angels, seven trumpets → \"another cycle of seven\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 3</b>: another angel with <b>golden censer</b> at the altar</li><li class=\"d1\">given much <b>incense</b> to offer with the <b>prayers of all the saints</b></li><li class=\"d1\">on the <b>golden altar</b> before the throne</li></ul>"},{"t":979.57,"lv":3,"h":"Altars and the throne","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Which altar? <b>Altar of incense</b> - several altars in Torah</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Altar of incense</b>: horned, in the <b>holy place</b>, in front of the curtain</li><li class=\"d1\">where priests did most business: <b>morning and evening</b> incense with prayers</li><li class=\"d1\">\"first commandment about worship in the Torah\" → <b>Matins and Vespers</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Altar of burnt offering</b>: in the <b>courtyard</b>, outside</li><li class=\"d1\">huge amounts of greasy smoke - \"didn't work so well inside a tent of goat hair\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Throne of God</b> at back of the most holy place; <b>altar of incense = his footstool</b></li><li class=\"d1\">our church set up the same: <b>high place</b> behind the altar</li><li class=\"d1\">blessing the high place; priest stands <b>off to the side</b> - <b>Christ enthroned in the middle</b></li><li class=\"d0\">In heaven: <b>no curtain</b>; altar of incense, <b>solid gold</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1116.99,"lv":2,"h":"8:3-5 - The censer thrown to earth","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Incense altar: <b>coal burning all the time</b>, incense offered on it</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Censers</b> make it <b>mobile</b></li><li class=\"d1\">coal and incense in censer → carry to <b>purify space</b>, even outside</li><li class=\"d0\">Angel takes <b>coal and incense</b> in the gold censer</li><li class=\"d1\">incense = <b>prayers of all the saints</b></li><li class=\"d1\">so the <b>prayers of the saints</b> are going to purify something</li><li class=\"d1\">same saints just seen serving, offering prayers and intercessions</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 4-5</b>: smoke ascends before God; angel fills censer with altar fire, <b>throws it to the earth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">noises, thunderings, lightnings, <b>earthquake</b> - \"sensor smash\"</li><li class=\"d1\">purifying <b>the earth</b> - \"kind of a violent purification\"</li><li class=\"d1\">again: incense = <b>prayers of the saints</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1257.87,"lv":2,"h":"Trumpets: ritual purification of sacred space","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Seals = about <b>authority</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ taking back <b>authority over creation</b>, authority to <b>judge</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Trumpets = focus on <b>ritual purification</b></li><li class=\"d1\">turning the creation back into <b>sacred space</b>, as it was originally</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Genesis 1</b>: seven days patterned after <b>ancient Near East temple dedication rituals</b></li><li class=\"d1\">seventh day God \"rests\" - read too literally, \"needed a break\"</li><li class=\"d1\">rests = <b>sat down</b> = <b>enthroned</b> in his temple, the whole cosmos</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Temple got defiled</b> - \"not doing so great right now\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Before: saints in <b>heavenly temple</b>, of which earth's was a copy</li><li class=\"d0\">Now: <b>earth becomes where God dwells</b>, whole creation, not just heavens</li></ul>"},{"t":1374.03,"lv":2,"h":"8:6-9 - First two trumpets","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Seven angels prepare to sound</li><li class=\"d0\">Trumpet = <b>shofar</b>, ram's horn - not the \"long skinny\" one on a Mormon church</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>First</b>: <b>hail and fire mingled with blood</b> thrown to the earth</li><li class=\"d1\">a <b>third of trees</b> burned, all green grass</li><li class=\"d1\">Q: where in the Bible? → <b>plague on Egypt</b> - hail and fire together</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Second</b>: something like a <b>great burning mountain</b> thrown into the sea</li><li class=\"d1\">a <b>third of the sea became blood</b>, third of sea creatures died, third of ships destroyed</li><li class=\"d1\">Egypt again - <b>water turned to blood</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1498.94,"lv":3,"h":"8:10-12 - Third and fourth trumpets","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Third</b>: great star falls, burning like a torch, on <b>a third of rivers and springs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">star's name <b>Wormwood</b>; third of waters bitter; many die</li><li class=\"d1\">not directly an Egypt plague - but <b>bitter water at Sinai</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Moses throws the wood</b> in, becomes sweet</li><li class=\"d1\">notice <b>a third</b> again</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Fourth</b>: a third of <b>sun, moon, stars</b> darkened; third of day and night without light</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>darkness over Egypt</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Can't be in <b>strict order</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sixth seal: all stars fell, sun darkened, moon blood - now back to <b>a third</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"literally impossible\" as a succession of future events → <b>overlapping cycles</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1605.6,"lv":2,"h":"8:13 - Triple woe","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 13</b>: angel flying in midst of heaven: <b>woe, woe, woe</b> to inhabitants of earth for the <b>three remaining trumpets</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Pause: \"you're really in trouble, it's about to get worse\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Looking from <b>purification</b>: looks like the opposite</li><li class=\"d1\">\"purification with an engine\" - things keep getting smote, a third of them</li><li class=\"d1\">stuff falling from sky: mountains, stars, meteors</li><li class=\"d0\">The <b>third</b> is important</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Revelation 12</b>: dragon throws <b>a third of the stars of heaven</b> down (not tonight)</li><li class=\"d1\">thirds + <b>Egypt plagues</b> = tip-off</li></ul>"},{"t":1704.08,"lv":2,"h":"The Passover: judging the gods of Egypt","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Before the final plague, <b>Passover</b> - death of the firstborn</li><li class=\"d0\">God tells Moses <b>two things</b> he'll do that night</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1. Judge all the gods of Egypt</b></li><li class=\"d1\">tip-off: from Exodus, they're <b>not fictional characters</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"doesn't need to judge the <b>Marvel Cinematic Universe</b>... Star Wars\" - fiction</li><li class=\"d1\">gods include <b>Pharaoh</b>; <b>demonic powers</b> control Egypt, people followed and worshipped them</li><li class=\"d1\">judging them to liberate <b>his people</b> - and <b>any Egyptians who want</b> out</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>2. Make a distinction</b> between Egypt and Israel</li></ul>"},{"t":1790.37,"lv":3,"h":"What the distinction means","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Already a distinction: plagues didn't fall on <b>Goshen</b></li><li class=\"d1\">darkness, water to blood, frogs - everywhere <b>except where Israelites lived</b></li><li class=\"d1\">but Israelites and Egyptians lived <b>right next to each other</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Egyptians in Israelite neighborhoods \"lucked out\" - scot free</li><li class=\"d0\">Now: <b>instructions given</b>; some follow, some don't</li><li class=\"d0\">Whoever follows = <b>Israelite</b>; whoever doesn't = <b>Egyptian</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't matter <b>DNA, skin color, great-great-grandfather</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Celebrate Passover = now an Israelite</b></li><li class=\"d1\">rest of Torah: <b>circumcised</b>, then celebrate Passover</li><li class=\"d1\">woman: marry a circumcised man, <b>eat the Passover</b></li><li class=\"d0\">→ distinction between people of God and those of <b>other spirits being judged</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1938.86,"lv":2,"h":"Why a third: separating sides","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">John wants us thinking of the <b>Egypt plagues</b> and that distinction</li><li class=\"d1\">that's why <b>a third</b> - a <b>separation</b> is happening</li><li class=\"d0\">Creation = God's <b>temple</b>; first thing that defiled it? <b>The devil</b> - the serpent</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not a literal snake\" (\"snake walker\")</li><li class=\"d0\">Adam and Eve should have <b>run him out of town</b></li><li class=\"d1\">protected and purified the <b>sacred space</b>; instead <b>sided with him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">through their death he got <b>ownership rights</b></li><li class=\"d0\">To purify sacred space: <b>separate who's on which side</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Chapter 12 number of demonic spirits = <b>a third</b></li><li class=\"d1\">people allied with them probably also about a third</li><li class=\"d1\">plagues fall on them</li></ul>"},{"t":2048.81,"lv":3,"h":"Mixed multitude and the chance to repent","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Egypt: distinction not made <b>until the last plague</b></li><li class=\"d1\">watching first nine plagues, Moses vs Pharaoh, an Egyptian could decide: <b>Yahweh is the one I want to follow</b></li><li class=\"d1\">at Passover: opportunity to <b>leave with them</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"Mixed multitude\"</b> comes out of Egypt</li><li class=\"d1\">people with <b>Egyptian names</b> - like <b>Moses</b>, and his family</li><li class=\"d1\">ethnically <b>completely mixed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God <b>creating a new people</b> that didn't exist before</li><li class=\"d0\">Nine plagues could have driven them to <b>repentance</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why in sequence? \"Kill all the wicked. Done.\" - not how God does it; <b>step by step</b></li><li class=\"d1\">people <b>observing</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2159.07,"lv":2,"h":"Every judgment is a call to repentance","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Angel with the woes</b> calling out to somebody</li><li class=\"d1\">warning it's about to get worse: <b>\"now's the time to switch sides\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Like the seals: <b>Christ taking back authority</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>every judgment is a call to repentance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">tribulation can become the <b>cause of repentance</b> → join the <b>white-robed number</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same from <b>sacred space</b> perspective</li><li class=\"d1\">why God doesn't just \"boom, it's done\"</li><li class=\"d1\">he <b>extends this period</b> for opportunities to repent</li><li class=\"d0\">Aside: the <b>third</b> in history</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Black Plague</b>; <b>Thirty Years' War</b> killed about a third</li><li class=\"d1\">people always saying \"a third of Europe, this is it\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not literal - points to <b>other spirits besides the Holy Spirit</b> animating people</li><li class=\"d0\">God not just destroying and punishing but giving <b>opportunity to repent</b> until the point <b>repentance is closed</b></li></ul>"}],"next":"Next week: <b>Revelation 9</b> - the final trumpets; then <b>Enoch and Elijah</b> back, people eating books"});
